course: dictionary
lesson: 9661
title: Layers under our feet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Soil is not one single layer. Dig a hole in a garden and you can see stripes of different colours, one above another. The layer just under the top layer is called subsoil. «Dark topsoil» sits on top, and «paler subsoil» lies below it. The word sub means under, so subsoil is the soil under the topsoil.
explain: Topsoil has the most humus and the most life. Humus is the dark, rotted-down material left from dead plants and animals. Subsoil has less humus, so it is often paler and harder. Below the subsoil comes solid rock, called bedrock. «Topsoil is the dark upper layer with the most humus and life; below it lie subsoil and then solid rock.»
explain: Subsoil matters because plants and people use it. Plant roots grow down into the subsoil to find water. Gardeners and builders dig into it too. You may also meet clay subsoil, which is one common kind you can find when you dig.
fact: Subsoil is the layer of soil under the topsoil.
fact: Subsoil has less humus than topsoil, and it is often harder.
fact: Subsoil lies above the bedrock.
fact: Plant roots go down into the subsoil to find water.
exercise: Which layer is the dark, crumbly layer on top? | Subsoil | Bedrock | *Topsoil
exercise: Where is the subsoil found in the soil? | In the air above the garden | Inside the bedrock | Above the topsoil, right at the top | *Under the topsoil
exercise: Where do plant roots go to find water? | Up into the air | Into the topsoil and then out of the ground | *Down into the subsoil | Only into the topsoil, never deeper
test: Which layer has the most humus and life? | Clay | *Topsoil | Subsoil | Bedrock
test: Which layer is at the very bottom of the soil layers? | Humus | Subsoil | Topsoil | *Bedrock
exam: Which statement about subsoil is true? | It is the layer above the topsoil | It is solid rock at the very bottom | *It lies under the topsoil and has less humus | It is the top layer with the most humus
